// @PLN25 slice (c) — (N-Store) at the RETURN site, the VIOLATION cells.
// Each function alone is a COMPILE ERROR gate-ON (LOFT_PLN25_DN3=1):
//   "a nullable `integer?` cannot be stored into the return value of the
//    non-null type `integer` — discharge it first with `?? <default>` or `match`"
// Gate-OFF the `?` is a no-op and these silently return `null` (the pre-fix
// behaviour the teeth replace).  Uncomment ONE function + its `main` call to see
// the diagnostic (two in one file would just report the first).

// R1: explicit return of an un-discharged `integer?` into a non-null return.
// fn r1(x: integer?) -> integer { return x; }

// R4: implicit tail — an un-discharged `integer?` is the function's last expr.
// fn r4(x: integer?) -> integer { x }

fn main() { print("uncomment a violation above"); }
